export anchor BlueprintStyle:
    number: 7
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Blueprint
    idea: The dashboard as an engineering drawing on pale blue drafting paper, with navy line work, monospace lettering, outlined boxes and dimension style annotations.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #e9f2fc, the page under the grid
        gridMinor: #d6e5f6, the 8px background grid
        gridMajor: #bcd4ee, the 40px background grid and chart guide lines
        wash: #f4f8fd, the fill inside every box
        navy: #0b2a5b, text, the sheet frame, box outlines and the primary button
        lineBlue: #1d5fa8, rules, table lines, progress fill, open chart bars and links
        cyan: #2a9fd6, decoration only and never text
        pencil: #3c5a80, captions, labels and meta text
        green: #0b6146, the On track status
        amber: #8a5300, the At risk status
        redline: #b0213a, the Behind status, the overdue count and the overdue note
        trace: #fff7d6, the focus fill
    type:
        One monospace family for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono,
        Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas, Liberation Mono, monospace. Sizes
        are 44px bold summary figures, a 30px bold greeting, 22px brand
        in caps with 0.18em tracking, 13px bold caps figure titles with
        0.14em tracking, 14px body at 1.5 and 11px caps captions with
        0.14em tracking.
    layout:
        A drawing sheet capped at 1280px with a 2px navy outer frame and a
        1px blue inner frame. At the top a title block grid lists Project
        Brightwork, Drawing Home Overview, Drawn by Mara Okafor, the date
        and Sheet 01 of 06. A tool row holds the search, the bell and New
        project, then the nav as numbered sheet tabs 01 to 06. A General
        Notes box holds the greeting as a numbered list beside a summary
        strip whose labels sit on dimension lines with end ticks. Below,
        FIG. 1 PROJECT SCHEDULE is a full width ruled table with refs P-01
        to P-06 and a key. FIG. 2 THROUGHPUT and FIG. 3 ACTIVITY LOG sit
        side by side. Every figure title is set into the top border of its
        box. Below 1000px everything stacks, the title block becomes two
        columns and the table scrolls inside its box.
    spacing: An 8px unit matching the minor grid. 24px between figures and 16 to 24px inside.
    density: Medium. 40px table rows and figures packed like a drawing sheet.
    corners: Square. Only the initial tags and the status rings are round.
    borders: A 2px navy sheet frame, a 1px blue inner frame, 1px navy figure boxes, 1px blue table cells and 1px dashed blue dividers.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Outline drafting icons with a 1.5px stroke. Status is a ringed dot
        for On track, an open triangle with a bar for At risk and a
        crossed square for Behind, beside the word in caps. The chart uses
        open outlined bars for last week and hatched bars for this week,
        with dimension lines marking each week total and a leader to MAX
        17. People show as outlined circle initials.
    focus: A 2px dashed navy outline offset 3px with the trace fill.
    tone: Technical drawing language with caps labels, FIG. numbers, refs such as P-04, and times written as T minus 12 min.
